WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.170
It'll be delivered tomorrow, then? 
Okay, thank you very much.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.520
Okay, that takes care of the orders.

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.990
Good work.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.730
Which do you want?

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.270
Only three days until 
the school festival, huh...

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.910
Time sure does fly, doesn't it?

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.040
It does.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.040
Yeah! I'm going to figure 
something out, damn it!

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>Nanako started practicing 
singing seriously after that.</i>

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.090
<i>With the help of Sugimoto-senpai, 
from the music program...</i>

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.550
<i>She's been re-learning pitch 
and vocalization from the basics,</i>

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.080
<i>building the stamina 
it takes to sing... and...</i>

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.060
Okay. This is where it starts.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Guide Desk</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>400 yen</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Menu</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Coffee</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Anmitsu</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Tapioca</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>Teahouse</b>

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.270
Time really does fly.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.390
Hey, Kyoya...

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:26.650
Do you think I'll really be 
able to sing if I keep this up?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.910
I mean, it's not that 
I don't like the practice!

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.040
And I can tell it's helping!

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.050
But... But still...

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.840
I'm wondering, what exactly will be 
the result of all this hard work?

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.840
You mean, like a goal?

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.430
Yeah. I'm not really sure 
what mine is anymore.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.980
It's okay for me 
to keep doing this, isn't it?

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.240
You should!

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.990
You've finally found something 
you can get serious about.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.900
It'd be a waste if you didn't keep going.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.270
I mean, I only got a taste 
of how serious you are,

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.360
and it was enough to move me!

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.970
Kyoya...

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:07.720
Why do you care so much 
about what I do, Kyoya?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.250
Because I heard your singing, Nanako!

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.830
It'd have that effect on anybody!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:18.360
If you're really not sure what you want, 
I'll help you find a goal...

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.720
And do everything I can to help.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.510
Until you're satisfied, 
I swear I'll figure something out!

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.110
Thank you, Kyoya!

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.930
I'm so grateful.

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.110
I've never had a friend who'd 
go this far for me before.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.620
Uh, s-sorry!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.010
That was just...

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.030
I honestly just felt grateful, 
and ended up, sorta...

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.460
You know how it is, right?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:56.330
People get all worked up 
at school festivals!

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.780
A-Anyway, don't get the wrong idea!

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.170
But, thanks. I feel better now.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.100
Okay.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:10.740
<i>Nanako, Shinoaki, 
Tsurayuki, and Kawasegawa...</i>

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.560
<i>There are a lot of amazing people around me.</i>

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.690
<i>They're all struggling to create something 
amazing in spite of their own troubles.</i>

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:23.000
<i>I think I was sent here 
from ten years in the future</i>

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.110
<i>to help them make it happen.</i>

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.980
It's kind of impressive.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.960
Yeah, tell me about it!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.760
<i>The Oonaka University of Arts School Festival
 takes place over three days,</i>

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.570
<i>and is a famous 
and storied event in Kansai.</i>

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.400
<i>There's all the typical concessions 
stands you'd expect,</i>

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.660
<i>along with art exhibitions 
and independent film screenings.</i>

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.250
<i>Along with serious music performances.</i>

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.030
<i>It brings in visitors from all over.</i>

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.940
"Then I shall present this to you!"

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:02.940
<b>The Red Forest</b>

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.490
A period play?

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.750
Yeah! I'm gonna be acting in it, too!

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.560
You gotta come check it out! See ya!

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.990
I wonder how our setup is going.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.330
<b>Maid</b>

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:15.330
<b>Café</b>

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.540
Welcome home, Master!

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.380
I-I'm back?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.020
Come on! Quit staring!

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.250
It's embarrassing.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.680
Sorry!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.670
Howzzat? Pretty sweet, right?

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:33.770
Keiko-san?! What are you doing here?

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.930
I heard there weren't enough people, so...

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.770
Whatcha think? Am I one hell 
of a loli maid, or what?

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.540
You're perfect!

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.580
Well, then... guess you owe me double now.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.910
The maids here are 
supposed to be super cute!

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:52.680
I actually came here instead 
of checking out the movies.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.410
Pretty well thought-out, considering that
 students are running things.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.410
<b>Order of Admission Ticket</b>

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.000
Do I order now?

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.420
Can I get your order, please?

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.810
A milkshake with extra cuteness, 
and a bittersweet love coffee float.

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:07.590
Will that complete your order?

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:09.890
Be really tasty!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:14.430
Onii-chan, make sure to eat up 
my love before it gets cold!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.430
<b>Money</b>

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:26.530
Sorry that you ended up having to cook
 and handle all of the orders.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.840
It's okay.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.370
Sugimoto-san and Kakihara-san are on
 the committee that's running the concert.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.480
I need to do what I can.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.570
Did you hear that? 
Maybe learn a lesson from—

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.120
Good... Very good...

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.330
Work, damn you!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.090
No! My art—

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.010
How is this art, you dirty old man?!

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.550
What is it?

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:58.480
You had a little rice on your cheek.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.570
Th... Thanks...

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:02.730
You're very welcome.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:06.270
<i>In spite of it all, the maid café 
was a huge success.</i>

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:09.910
<i>We ended up working all day, 
two days in a row,</i>

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:12.200
<i>without a chance to check out 
the rest of the festival.</i>

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.740
I'm home...

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:17.350
Damn, what happened to you guys?

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.370
Welcome home.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.530
I am so tired.

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:25.680
Is being a maid heavy labor, or something?

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.900
We were basically packed all day.

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:30.990
Which is good, but it didn't
 leave us much time to rest.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:35.240
And tomorrow's the last day.

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.610
This feels more like overtime 
at work than a festival.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:44.100
Sorry. But considering we hit 
our sales goal in just two days,

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.760
I'll talk to our senpais and ask 
about closing early tomorrow.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:49.780
Please do!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.470
You should come and check it out, Tsurayuki.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.800
It's been a bigger deal 
than I thought, and pretty fun.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.270
Yeah, man! It's gotta be boring, 
working all the time.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.330
You owe yourself a change of pace.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:03.200
I'm not feeling bad enough 
that I need a change.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.810
But I definitely have to check this out.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:10.010
<b>The First Film Directed by Inugiri Waichi
Banquet of Sadists</b>

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:10.670
And maybe I'll check out the ex-gangster 
Kogure-chan's maid look while I'm—

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:12.330
I am <i>not</i> an ex-gangster!

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:14.460
I told you to quit it with the jokes!

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.390
Plus, if you want to come, just admit it!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.940
It's not going to kill you 
to be honest, is it?

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.720
Wrong! I have a totally 
different motivation here!

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:28.400
Fine, you don't get to ever see me 
dressed up like a maid, then!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.650
<b>Final Day</b>

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:35.850
The maid café... this is it.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.500
Kawasegawa?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.370
You came to the festival?

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.900
You probably think 
I don't fit in, don't you?

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.170
I didn't say that.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:46.460
I just didn't think you'd come by 
unless you had a reason.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:49.480
I think I understand 
your image of me now.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.300
Not that you're wrong, but still...

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.630
<b>The first film directed by Inugiri Waichi
Banquet of Sadists</b>

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.260
I thought I'd drop by, 
since I came to see this.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.930
Plus... well...

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.930
I wanted to apologize to her.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.420
To Nanako?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.240
I don't think you need to.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.350
Why not?

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:11.550
Because she's starting 
to take singing seriously now.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:15.030
What you said to her was the trigger.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.010
Then it was a waste of effort to come here?

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:22.770
But since you're here already, 
you might as well—

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.310
Why on earth would I?

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.610
I have no interest in moe-moe pancakes—

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:32.170
E-Er, anyway, the movie 
is starting soon. I need to get going.

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.210
Kawasegawa!

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:38.940
You should listen to Nanako sing someday.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:43.550
Right. Especially if she's 
gotten serious about it.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:52.020
Sasuke! I bear you no grudge, 
but you will die here!

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.410
Damn you, Eisai...

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.820
I wonder where Hikawa-kun is.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.910
He said he would be performing, but...

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:08.550
<i>And thus, Sasuke died in the street, 
exhausted and wounded.</i>

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.530
<i>And only the great tree 
where he finally fell</i>

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:14.710
<i>stood to mark his passing!</i>

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:14.710
Kyoya-kun, look!

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:33.410
That's the fine arts program for you. 
This is all pretty serious stuff.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:41.870
<i>This is impressive.</i>

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.370
<i>The composition is well thought-out...</i>

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.470
<i>The sense of atmosphere is delicate 
to the point of transparency...</i>

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.500
<i>It'd make a good match for Shinoaki's art.</i>

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.210
<i>Who made it?</i>

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.790
<i>Yamashina Kazu?</i>

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:57.390
<i>Where have I heard that name before?</i>

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:01.050
<b>Yamashina Kazu

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:01.050
<i>Wait... I feel dizzy...</i>

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:05.480
Kyoya-kun?

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:07.200
Kyoya-kun, what's wrong?

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.310
Kyoya-kun! Kyoya-kun?!

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.430
What's up? Already closed?

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:20.640
Too bad for you!

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.150
You missed out on all 
those moe-moe kyun girls.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.260
I'll have to settle for you, then.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.940
That's rude!

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:38.090
Kyoya-kun, you feeling okay?

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:44.340
You've been working non-stop... 
must have been real tired.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:47.970
Sh-Shinoaki?!

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.410
Uh...

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:52.690
Just sit still.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:02.930
This is kinda embarrassing, 
so let me just say it.

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.590
Kyoya-kun, you're real grown up, 
and can do anything.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:11.700
I think it's amazing.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:16.160
I was really glad about what 
you said, back then, too.

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.630
About how I can't stop, 
and how you love my art.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.660
I...

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.280
Shinoaki?

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:34.940
Sorry.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.080
Hello?

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.360
They're calling for me?

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.360
The closing act didn't show?!

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.280
How did this happen?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.070
They were double-booked.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.450
<b>Aurora Clarity</b>

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.450
<b>Miracle Portrait</b>

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.450
<b>Seraffi 1st Class</b>

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.450
<b>Prince of Purrsia</b>

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.450
<b>Secret Guest</b>

00:12:48.070 --> 00:12:50.450
We expected Mori Shogo 
to be among the guests.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.580
No way! Isn't that...

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:55.240
That's not the kind of artist you'd get 
at most school festivals.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.580
Yeah.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.890
But we were lucky enough to talk 
to him before he went on hiatus.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:03.890
We got word of him accepting, too.

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:06.890
But now we're hearing that he'll be a no-show.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:11.390
Apparently it's at the same time as 
the filming of some music program for TV.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.860
And since he was going to be a secret guest,

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.520
they say to just put someone else on!

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:17.560
Damn it!

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.370
In that case...

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:24.530
I figure you just gotta put 
someone else on, instead.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:29.200
It's not that easy! Who could 
we get, this close to showtime?

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.000
What're you, dense?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.940
This is a freakin' art school.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:35.750
It's crawling with people who wanna sing.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:40.740
Listen...

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:41.900
Sup?

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:44.340
What about having Nanako sing?

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:52.760
That was Prince of Purrsia!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:57.780
Next, after a fifteen-minute intermission, 
our secret guest will be up!

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:01.110
You'll have to stick around 
to see who it is!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.710
K-Kyoya, you're joking, right?

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.840
No, I'm not.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:09.010
You're the only one who can do this.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:11.450
Let's use the fact that you never 
publicized who it was to our advantage.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.450
A backing band with an unknown singer...

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.440
That would explain why 
it was listed as a secret.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.620
But...

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.880
I think Nanako can pull it off.

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.670
It's still rough around the edges,

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.810
but her voice has a power to resonate 
directly with the listener's heart.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:29.090
It hasn't been long, 
but I've been teaching her right.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:33.710
But if this fails, it could 
ruin the entire show.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.350
If she's going to do this, 
she needs to be prepared.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.440
Right. I understand.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:41.870
I'll go talk to the backing band.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:48.450
This has turned into a whole thing, huh?

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.880
I... I can't...

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.350
Nanako?

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:57.790
Singing in front of people, all of a sudden? 
And in the place of a pro?

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.580
There's no way I can manage that.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.500
Nanako, it's okay. I know you can—

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.250
I can see it.

00:15:07.870 --> 00:15:13.480
Everyone saying how terrible I am... 
Laughing about me even showing up.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:16.330
I'm scared. I'm too scared!

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.520
Nanako!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.510
I'll bring her back, I promise!

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.390
Whoa, man!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.660
Buy time until we get back! Please!

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:25.860
Buy time? Us?

00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:30.500
<i>When opportunities appear, they always seem 
like they're going to be impossible at first.</i>

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:33.820
<i>My extra ten years of experience 
have taught me that.</i>

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:38.460
<i>I know how bitter it feels think 
about "If I had only..."</i>

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:41.620
<i>I don't want that for you, Nanako!</i>

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:47.470
What do you mean, 
the replacement act ran away?!

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:49.760
There are only ten minutes 
left in the intermission!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.840
It's all right. Nanako will show, 
and she will sing.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:59.730
That girl... is not the kind of person 
to let pressure keep her from performing.

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.810
I guarantee you.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.950
How does your guarantee help?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:05.980
I'll keep the crowd warm in the meantime.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:12.210
The visual arts first-year, 
Rokuonji Tsurayuki is, in reality...

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:14.990
A traveling clown.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:20.280
You knew where I had been practicing, huh?

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:21.540
Of course.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:25.490
I understand in my head. 
This is a big chance.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:29.930
A way to confront everything 
I've been putting off all along.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:36.340
But... confronting it 
means potentially losing.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:40.970
And if I lose this time... 
If I lose when I'm serious, then...

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:43.560
It's okay. You won't lose, Nanako.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.790
Why?! How can you be so sure, Kyoya?!

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:52.970
Because you've practiced so much.

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:54.200
No...

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.490
It doesn't matter how much you practice... 
an actual performance is different.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:03.660
I can't sing in front of people. 
Not in front of a crowd of hundreds...

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:07.810
The idea of that many people judging me...

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.710
It's terrifying.

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:13.760
Right now, I'm seriously terrified.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.810
This isn't like it was before.

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:19.970
No one's going to go, "That was bad, but kind
 of impressive," or, "You're almost there."

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.700
Excuses won't cut it.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:26.840
I'm so scared about it, I feel 
like I'm going to fall apart.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:30.160
You're scared because you're serious.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:32.360
Because you're taking singing seriously.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:37.740
Remember, I said I would figure 
something out to help you.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:41.460
Damn it! How can you be so sure, Kyoya?!

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.410
Because of this.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:52.210
Wow, that is something!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:55.230
Now, everyone, let's have 
a round of applause!

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:59.220
<i>Crap, I'm out of tricks...</i>

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.900
<i>Kyoya, how long is this supposed to take?</i>

00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:03.260
Tsurayuki!

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:11.460
Okay, that has been a few magic tricks 
by a first-year who decided to pop in!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:16.470
Next up is the performance by our 
secret guest you've all been waiting for!

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.470
Don't run again, okay?

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:21.890
Like I would!

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:24.740
I'm gonna get a hundred times 
the applause you pulled off.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.640
I'm rooting for you!

00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:27.600
Right!

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:31.290
Watch me from the crowd, okay?

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:33.040
Got it.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:42.800
And here's our guest!

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:55.530
Huh? A maid?

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:56.820
Is this a performance art thing?

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:13.390
I wasn't really supposed to be singing 
here today, but some things came up.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:18.510
And I'd have to be stupid 
to turn down a chance like this, so...

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:26.100
Let's make sure to enjoy the finale 
of the school festival's concert!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:45.660
<i>I rush past you with a heart that's run dry</i>

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:52.660
<i>I'm sorry, but there's nothing else I can do</i>

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:58.320
<i>Because even sharing your pain</i>

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:06.140
<i>Is something you want to keep from me</i>

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:12.140
<i>To not ruin what we had, 
I couldn't look back</i>

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:17.650
<i>As I turned away and took 
my leave on the lonely rail</i>

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:21.990
<i>Following you no matter how much it hurts</i>

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.990
<i>This is it, right, Kyoya?</i>

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:24.710
<i>There was no reason to be scared!</i>

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:25.290
<i>Even in the darkest parts of the world</i>

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:25.990
<i>Because I'm...</i>

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:31.580
<i>Because I know you'll be there 
shining through into the future!</i>

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:29.830
Your new video broke ten thousand views!

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:32.320
I only uploaded it yesterday.

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:34.840
<i>And because I know my weakness,</i>

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:37.130
<b><u>Seeji
</u>This made me feel better!! You're only to going to get better from here

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:40.000
<b><u>Saito
</u>I seriously love the way your huskiness comes out on the high pitched parts</b>

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.840
You've already sung in front 
of thousands of people...

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:38.230
<i>I'll fight to keep my soul for breaking;</i>

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:40.840
<b><u>Rua
</u>Ahhhh! So good! I love it!

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:41.950
If you ask me, it doesn't make any 
sense to be afraid of a few hundred.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:43.090
<i>I'll do it my way, 
and as our moments overlap...</i>

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:47.610
<i>God bless the both of us</i>

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:48.970
Come on. I'm sure they'll 
all become fans of yours.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:55.270
<i>You were there, 
and I was there, and everyone else</i>

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.670
Yeah!

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.230
<i>Had seemed to disappear</i>

00:20:55.700 --> 00:21:00.280
<i>I know the world's not so simple that hard work 
is enough to get you where you want to be...</i>

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:08.840
<i>As I tried to create 
the beauty of a fleeting dream</i>

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.080
<i>But!</i>

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.680
<i>I want my feelings to reach them!</i>

00:21:06.850 --> 00:21:08.070
Not bad at all.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:10.890
This is what Nanako can do 
when she's serious.

00:21:08.840 --> 00:21:13.800
<i>I ran a finger across my scars</i>

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:15.540
So? What kind of trick 
did you use this time?

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.550
<i>And that is why I will be</i>

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.960
I wouldn't call it a trick...

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:19.480
<i>Following you no matter how much it hurts</i>

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:21.210
The videos we uploaded got 
a bigger response than I anticipated.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:22.980
<i>Even in the darkest parts of the world</i>

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:24.410
<i>Granted, there were negative comments, too.</i>

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:29.470
<i>Because I know you'll be there,
 shining through into the future!</i>

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:29.470
<i>But Nanako's voice drew in a lot 
more people than it turned away.</i>

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.440
<i>Nanako didn't run away.</i>

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.450
<i>And because I know my weakness,</i>

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:38.350
<b>○ Poor enunciation on H-sounds

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>She kept an open mind 
about even the harshest criticisms...</i>

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.860
<i>I'll fight to keep my soul for breaking</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:38.350
<i>And incorporated the advice she got 
into the next video she uploaded.</i>

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:41.000
<i>I'll do it my way, 
and as our moments overlap...</i>

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:43.460
<i>On the internet, artists and fans collaborate 
to make music through feedback.</i>

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:45.360
<i>God bless the both of us</i>

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:48.370
<i>And in ten years, when this they dub 
this kind of thing "user generated content"...</i>

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:52.370
<i>Nanako will have gained wings of song.</i>

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.370
<i>The first time I heard this voice, 
it captured my heart.</i>

00:21:56.890 --> 00:22:00.630
<i>I wasn't sure why, but now I understand.</i>

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:04.010
<i>It's nice to meet you, N@NA.</i>

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:11.180
And that completes the program 
for our music festival!

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:14.770
Goodbye everyone, and thanks for coming!

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:20.050
Kyoya, I did it! I managed to sing!

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:22.730
Huh? Where is he?

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.960
Good work out there.

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:26.250
Kyoya's still in the seats, probably.

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.570
Oh, right.

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:29.970
I need to thank him! Gotta find him first!

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:29.970
Hey!

00:22:34.650 --> 00:22:38.820
Sorry to drag you away 
from Nanako's encore...

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:41.870
It's fine. But are you okay?

00:22:41.870 --> 00:22:44.510
I thought maybe the crowd got to you.

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:46.670
Yeah, I'm feeling better now.

00:22:48.930 --> 00:22:52.040
The school festival's over, huh?

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:53.020
Yeah.

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:56.070
What is it?

00:22:56.760 --> 00:23:01.560
I was just thinking how we're 
about the same height, like this.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:04.370
Oh, yeah. Now that you mention it...

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:15.080
Kinda... got carried away there.

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:17.500
What do you mean, kinda?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:20.460
Maybe it's because of the festival?

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.890
Is that... really it?
